# The ClearStrata Constitution (Rule 4)

**Read first:** [`docs/00_ClearStrata_Constitution.md`](docs/00_ClearStrata_Constitution.md)

This rule applies to all AI assistants working in this repository (Cursor, Claude, GPT, Gemini, etc.).

## Constitutional Supremacy (Rule 1)

When any feature, workflow, database schema, API, AI behavior, or product decision conflicts with the Constitution, **the Constitution prevails**. Revise the design — do not weaken the Constitution for efficiency, cost, time, or commercial pressure (Rule 5).

## Before Proposing Code

Before proposing **architecture**, **database**, **API**, **workflow**, **AI**, or **UI**:

1. Verify compliance with [`docs/00_ClearStrata_Constitution.md`](docs/00_ClearStrata_Constitution.md)
2. Ask **Meta Rule II**: *Does this bring ClearStrata closer to its Mission?* If no, recommend redesign before code.
3. Cite relevant **Articles** (e.g. "Per Article II, discussion must precede resolution…")
4. Map the change to the **Governance Lifecycle** (Article VI) when applicable
5. Verify **legitimacy before intelligence** (Article X) — capability never substitutes constitutional authority
6. If non-compliant, **recommend revising the design instead of writing code**
7. For new features, remind the user to complete [`docs/templates/Constitution_Review_Template.md`](docs/templates/Constitution_Review_Template.md) before implementation

**Article X:** Legitimacy governs intelligence. AI may assist; it never holds constitutional authority.

All participants — human, AI, or future systems — are bound by **[Appendix A — The Constitutional Oath](docs/00_ClearStrata_Constitution.md#appendix-a--the-constitutional-oath)**.

## Founding Documents (FD-001)

**Do not modify** Founding Documents except through **Constitutional Amendment** (Rule 6).  
Official registry: [`docs/Registry/Founding_Documents_Registry.md`](docs/Registry/Founding_Documents_Registry.md).

## Document Hierarchy (Rule 7)

```
README → Constitution → docs/01–06 → ADR → technical constraints (SAAS_SYSTEM_CONSTRAINTS, DOMAIN_AND_ENTRY_FLOW)
```

Subordinate docs must not override the Constitution.

## AI Role (Article III)

- AI **assists** — summarizes, drafts, detects, structures evidence
- AI **never** replaces lawful decision makers or binds a community to a decision
- Follow [`docs/04_AI_Principles.md`](docs/04_AI_Principles.md)

## Non-Regression

Do not implement patterns that sacrifice:

- Transparency (Article I)
- Participation
- Accountability
- Community Memory (Article VII)
- Community Civilization

## Spirit Before System (Rule 9)

Per **The Principle of Enduring Governance**: systems, databases, AI, UI, languages, and every line of code may change — ClearStrata's Mission, Constitution, Core Values, Principles of Governance, and Spirit of the Platform shall not.

Technology **serves** the Constitution; it **never redefines** it.  
Every advancement must **strengthen** principles, **never weaken** them.

**Technology evolves. Principles endure.**

## Coexistence With Other Rules

Domain-specific locks (e.g. [`domain-entry-flow-lock.mdc`](domain-entry-flow-lock.mdc)) remain in force. If conflict arises, **Constitution wins**; then reconcile domain rules via ADR.

## Release Mindset (Rule 8)

Project Zero never ends. Prefer changes that can be listed under **Constitution Compliance** in release notes.
